<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav December wages up 11.9 pct to 881 dinars.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav December wages up 11.9 pct to 881 dinars.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV AVERAGE NET WAGES   DEC 96    NOV 96    DEC 95</p>
<p> wage in dinars		     881	 787	 484</p>
<p> mth/mth pct change	     +11.9     -1.4	+15.0</p>
<p>NOTE -- The average wage for 1996 was 658 dinars.</p>
<p>The December '96 average wage was 82 percent higher than the average wage in December '95 in nominal terms, and 13.8 percent higher in real terms.</p>
<p>Data do not include private sector.</p>
<p>($1=5.4 dinars) -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
